= Autonomy [HV-01] =

//An enduring conception of a desirable state that matters to Stakeholders. A first-class grounding node.//

**Report Format:** §1.2 Human Values and Human Factors

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|HV-01
|Name|Autonomy
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Interviews/observations with residents and care staff
|Situated meaning|Autonomy means being able to participate in everyday activities and make choices for themselves, rather than having tasks automatically taken over by caregivers or technology. In daily activities such as brushing teeth or taking medication, this means allowing the person to initiate and perform the steps they are still capable of doing, while providing assistance or prompting only when needed.
|Held by|(((
ST-01: Resident with dementia

ST-02: Care home employee
)))
|Intrinsic or instrumental|It is an intrinsic value because having choice and control over one's own everyday activities is valuable in itself. It can also instrumentally support related values such as dignity and wellbeing.
|Recognition criteria|(((
Served: the person is given meaningful opportunities to make choices, initiate actions and perform steps independently. assistance or prompting is provided when needed rather than automatically taking over. 

Violated: choices are unnecessarily overridden, the resident is not given an opportunity to act independently, or caregivers/technology routinely take over activities the resident remains capable of performing.
)))
|Source|Self-Determination Theory

= Dignity  [HV-02] =

//An enduring conception of a desirable state that matters to Stakeholders. A first-class grounding node.//

**Report Format:** §1.2 Human Values and Human Factors

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|Stable identifier, unique within this entity type (e.g. HV-01, HV-02…).
|Name|A short, human-readable label for this instance.
|Status|Not Started / In Progress / Under Review / In Evaluation / Finalized.
|Evidence basis|How this knowledge was obtained — direct observation, interview, literature, secondary data, or proxy informant — flagged as provisional where it rests on anything other than direct contact with the Stakeholder group it describes. For a Measure or Evaluation Method, cite existing use in a validation study or authoritative literature (e.g. a validated-instrument source or textbook) instead.
|Situated meaning|what this value actually means in this domain, for these Stakeholders, in these Activities — not the dictionary sense of the label.
|Held by|Stakeholder ID(s), with relative priority per Stakeholder where these differ.
|Intrinsic or instrumental|worth having for its own sake, or because it leads to something else. If instrumental, name the value it serves.
|Recognition criteria|how anyone could tell, in practice, that this value has been served or violated. A value with no recognition criteria cannot ground a Claim.
|Source|the value theory, framework, or elicitation method this rests on.

